    "Additional Comments": "The patient, a 47-year-old African-American gentleman with locally advanced adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, has experienced significant weight loss and pain, which have been managed with gemcitabine and Abraxane. He underwent an ERCP with EUS, resulting in the placement of a plastic stent, later replaced by an uncovered metal stent due to biliary ductal obstruction. Post-procedure, he was treated with IV and oral antibiotics for an infection. He reports intermittent abdominal discomfort managed with oxycodone, improved appetite, weight gain, and some neuropathy in his hands. He is also dealing with hypertension and possible cancer family syndrome. The patient is seeking psycho-oncology support to cope with his disease and social and economic issues."
